  "name": "connect-kcap",
  "description": "This skill should be used when the user asks to \"connect kcap\", \"set up kcap\", \"install kcap\", \"log in to kcap\", \"reconnect kcap\", or pastes the npm package name @kurrent/kcap. Also recognizes the former name Capacitor, including \"connect Capacitor\" and \"log in to Capacitor\". Use when a kcap tool or skill fails because `kcap` is not installed or not signed in. Installs the kcap CLI and signs it in. On a Muse Assistant VM it also registers kcap's MCP servers as a custom connector, writes the `kcap` skill and keeps the sign-in warm with an hourly cron. On a Grok Bot cloud computer it also starts the watcher that records the account's chats.",
